   280→    slugs:
   281→      - shadow-init
   282→    title: Shadow Initialization
   283→    type: feature
   284→    status:
   285→      maturity: draft
   286→      implementation: implemented
   287→    priority: high
   288→    tags:
   289→      - infrastructure
   290→      - cli
   291→    description: |
   292→      kspec init creates shadow branch and worktree by default.
   293→
   294→      Steps:
   295→      1. Add .kspec/ to .gitignore and commit (fails if .gitignore is dirty)
   296→      2. Create git worktree at .kspec/ with orphan branch kspec-meta
   297→      3. Create initial manifest and structure in .kspec/
   298→      4. Initial commit on shadow branch
   299→    acceptance_criteria:
   300→      - id: ac-shadow-init-1
   301→        given: a git repository without shadow branch
   302→        when: kspec init runs
   303→        then: orphan branch kspec-meta is created
   304→      - id: ac-shadow-init-2
   305→        given: kspec init has run
   306→        when: checking .kspec/ directory
   307→        then: it is a valid git worktree pointing to kspec-meta
   308→      - id: ac-shadow-init-3
   309→        given: kspec init has run
   310→        when: checking git log
   311→        then: .gitignore change is committed to main branch
   312→      - id: ac-shadow-init-4
   313→        given: shadow branch already exists
   314→        when: kspec init runs again
   315→        then: it succeeds without error (idempotent)
   316→      - id: ac-shadow-init-5
   317→        given: .gitignore has uncommitted changes
   318→        when: kspec init runs
   319→        then: it fails with error explaining the issue
   320→    implements:
   321→      - "@cmd-init"
   322→    requirements:
