   449→    title: Shadow Recovery
   450→    type: feature
   451→    status:
   452→      maturity: draft
   453→      implementation: implemented
   454→    priority: high
   455→    tags:
   456→      - infrastructure
   457→      - reliability
   458→    description: |
   459→      Recovery mechanisms for shadow branch issues. Provides CLI commands for
   460→      diagnosing and repairing shadow branch problems.
   461→
   462→      Commands:
   463→      - `shadow status`: Check health of shadow branch
   464→      - `shadow repair`: Recreate worktree when branch exists but worktree broken
   465→      - `shadow log`: View recent commits on shadow branch
   466→
   467→      Handles common issues:
   468→      - Worktree directory deleted (recreate from existing branch)
   469→      - Worktree disconnected from git (remove and recreate)
   470→      - Stale worktree references in git
   471→    acceptance_criteria:
   472→      - id: ac-recovery-1
   473→        given: shadow branch exists but .kspec/ directory is deleted
   474→        when: kspec shadow repair runs
   475→        then: worktree is recreated from existing branch
   476→      - id: ac-recovery-2
   477→        given: .kspec/ exists but .git file is missing or corrupt
   478→        when: kspec shadow repair runs
   479→        then: worktree is removed and recreated
   480→      - id: ac-recovery-3
   481→        given: shadow branch does not exist
   482→        when: kspec shadow repair runs
   483→        then: it fails with error suggesting kspec init
   484→      - id: ac-recovery-4
   485→        given: shadow branch is healthy
   486→        when: kspec shadow repair runs
   487→        then: it succeeds without changes (idempotent)
   488→      - id: ac-recovery-5
   489→        given: shadow branch is healthy
   490→        when: kspec shadow status runs
   491→        then: it reports healthy status with all checks passing
   492→      - id: ac-recovery-6
   493→        given: shadow branch has issues
   494→        when: kspec shadow status runs
   495→        then: it reports the specific issue and suggests repair
   496→    requirements:
   497→      - _ulid: 01KF1VBR1XMKDJ0K5HYW7RWGQE
