   505→        description: |
   506→          kspec shadow repair
   507→
   508→          Re-establishes worktree if .kspec/ is deleted or corrupted:
   509→          - Recreates worktree link from .git/worktrees/.kspec
   510→          - Detects and reports common corruption scenarios
   511→          - Handles: stale locks, orphaned worktrees, detached HEAD
   512→
   513→          Acceptance criteria:
   514→          - Recovers from deleted .kspec/ directory
   515→          - Reports clear error if shadow branch itself is missing
   516→          - Idempotent (safe to run multiple times)
   517→        implements:
   518→          - "@shadow-recovery"
